The output is incredibly verbose as it shows the entire internal config struct u"," "," ## Main / Unreleased"," ","+### Ingester WAL entries records have a new version","+","+Ingesters now write WAL entries records as `WALRecordEntriesV4`, which adds the timestamp of the","+Kafka record the entries were ingested from. Older versions can't read this record version.","+If you roll an ingester back, it can't replay the WAL records written since the upgrade. It logs","+`Recovered from WAL segments with errors`, increments","+`loki_ingester_wal_corruptions_total{type=\"segment\"}`, and starts without them, so entries that","+were not flushed yet are lost. To avoid that, shut the ingester down with a flush before rolling","+back, for example with `/ingester/shutdown?flush=true`.","+"," ### Statistics in detected-field query responses"," "," The `/loki/api/v1/detected_fields` and `/loki/api/v1/detected_field/{name}/values` JSON"],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/sources/shared/configuration.md","lines":["@@ -3920,6 +3920,12 @@ wal:","   # CLI flag: -ingester.wal-disk-full-threshold","   [disk_full_threshold: <float> | default = 0.9]"," ","+  # Write WAL records as V4, which store the Kafka record timestamp. Older","+  # versions can't replay them. When disabled, records are written as V3 and V4","+  # timestamps are ignored on replay.","+  # CLI flag: -ingester.wal-record-v4-enabled","+  [record_v4_enabled: <boolean> | default = false]","+"," # Shard factor used in the ingesters for the in process reverse index. This MUST"," # be evenly divisible by ALL schema shard factors or Loki will not start."," # CLI flag: -ingester.index-shards"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/compactor/deletion/job_runner.go","lines":["@@ -170,10 +170,8 @@ func (jr *JobRunner) Run(ctx context.Context, job *grpc.Job) ([]byte, error) {"," \t\t\tfacade,"," \t\t\tnewChunkStart,"," \t\t\tnewChunkEnd,","+\t\t\tchks[0].IngestedAt,"," \t\t)","-\t\t/